WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
When a patient calls your practice, your team may

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.367
already be helping someone at the desk, taking another

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.133
call, or finishing for the evening.

00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:09.167
The patient still needs an answer.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.167
And an appointment inquiry can end before anyone has

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:13.467
had a useful conversation.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:17.267
Flow Audit is an AI phone agent configured around

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:17.833
your practice.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.033
In the recorded demonstration you'll see, it handles an

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:24.233
appointment inquiry, offers available times, and creates a

00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:25.433
booking in a connected calendar.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.833
It supports your front desk with agreed call workflows

00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:29.800
and human handoffs.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.333
If that could help your practice, book a fifteen-minute

00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:32.867
walkthrough.

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.800
We'll discuss your requirements, the investment, and whether

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.900
you're ready to move forward.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.200
Start with your own call records.

00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:42.067
What happens during busy periods, at lunch, and after

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:42.500
closing?

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.400
How many callers are reached later, how many book,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.533
and how many attend?

00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:47.967
Those are different measures.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.967
A missed call is not automatically a lost patient.

00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:54.933
For illustration only, suppose five additional appointments were

00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:57.900
attended, each with an assumed gross value of one

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:58.967
hundred and fifty dollars.

00:00:58.967 --> 00:01:01.500
That's seven hundred and fifty dollars in gross appointment

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.100
value, before costs.

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:06.567
These are hypothetical inputs, not Flow Audit's results or

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:07.000
a forecast.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.733
Actual revenue depends on attendance, treatment, collection and

00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:11.800
your practice's circumstances.

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.367
Use your own figures to judge the opportunity.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.533
Here's a recorded demonstration using Google Calendar.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:20.267
A new patient wants to register and arrange a

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.100
checkup.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.367
Listen as the agent clarifies the request, offers appointment

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.833
times, and confirms the selected booking.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:30.233
This recording includes short privacy beeps and edited

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:31.433
demonstration labels.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.667
[Phone ringing]

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:37.900
Thanks for

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.167
[Privacy beep]

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.567
I'm Liv, how can I help?

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.367
Hiya, I just wanted to ring in and book an appointment.

00:01:46.933 --> 00:01:48.533
Thanks, can you please tell me

00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:50.733
if this is for you or someone else?

00:01:50.733 --> 00:01:52.567
It's for me, I'm new in the area,

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.933
I want to register with the dentist

00:01:54.933 --> 00:01:56.533
and then get checked up as well.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:00.200
Got it, are you looking for

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.067
a new patient check-up appointment?

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:05.000
Also, do you have a day or time that suits you best?

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.833
Ideally today, if we could do later on today,

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:08.233
that'd be great and yeah,

00:02:08.233 --> 00:02:10.200
this would be a new patient check-up.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:17.533
The first available appointment this afternoon

00:02:17.533 --> 00:02:21.500
is at 2.30 or three in the afternoon or 3.30.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.967
Which one works for you?

00:02:22.967 --> 00:02:24.200
Can we do three o'clock?

00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:29.167
Thanks, may I have your full name

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:31.567
and the best phone number to reach you on please?

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.600
Yeah, my name is Tristan Adams

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.600
and the best number to reach me on is this one.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.067
[Contact detail privacy beep]

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.567
[Contact detail privacy beep]

00:02:48.533 --> 00:02:50.367
Your new patient check-up appointment

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:53.233
is booked for Wednesday, the 7th of October

00:02:53.233 --> 00:02:55.033
at 3pm.

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.767
The team has all your details

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:58.400
and looks forward to seeing you then.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.067
Is there anything else I can help with?

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:02.500
No, that would be all. Thank you. Bye-bye.

00:03:02.833 --> 00:03:05.167
You can see the appointment in the calendar and

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:06.067
the recorded request.

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:08.667
That's the workflow this example demonstrates.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:12.100
Your scheduling system, appointment types and forwarding

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.867
arrangements still need checking.

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:17.900
Compatibility is assessed and tested for your practice; it

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.700
isn't a promise that every system connects.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.833
Some calls need different rules.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.267
In this second recorded example, the agent asks about

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:27.600
warning signs, and the caller answers.

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.500
Is your son experiencing any swelling,

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.300
uncontrolled bleeding, trauma,

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.167
or trouble breathing or swallowing?

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.200
No, none of that.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.233
Just that he's complaining about his toothache,

00:03:39.233 --> 00:03:41.100
it’s causing him a headache and things of that nature.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:41.967
I just wanna get him checked out

00:03:41.967 --> 00:03:43.767
and make sure it's nothing too serious.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:47.200
That question is not evidence of a clinically validated

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.867
triage service or a completed emergency handoff.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:53.367
Your practice approves escalation instructions and human handoffs

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:54.167
before activation.

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.633
The agent supports your team within agreed rules; it

00:03:57.633 --> 00:03:59.033
doesn't replace clinical judgment.

00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:03.100
Privacy, patient-data and security requirements must also be

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.100
resolved for your setup.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.233
We confirm a deliverable scope, explain the investment and

00:04:08.233 --> 00:04:09.733
agree the implementation requirements.

00:04:10.633 --> 00:04:12.367
If those are clear and you're ready to proceed,

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.967
an agreement and initial payment start configuration.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.167
We then configure the workflow, test it with your

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:21.333
team, and activate forwarding only after your approval.

00:04:21.933 --> 00:04:25.500
Unresolved compatibility or review requirements are conditions to

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.533
settle before proceeding.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.833
Book your fifteen-minute Flow Audit walkthrough.

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:33.100
Bring the practice owner or someone authorized to purchase.

00:04:33.733 --> 00:04:36.200
You'll already have seen the demonstration, so the call

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.967
focuses on your practice: the relevant workflow, requirements,

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:41.100
scope and investment.

00:04:41.733 --> 00:04:43.733
If it's the right fit, we'll discuss getting your

00:04:43.733 --> 00:04:44.733
configuration started.

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.467
For a larger group, we can identify the approvals

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:48.767
and next decision needed.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.300
Book your walkthrough below.
